1
00:00:17,248 --> 00:00:24,964
Winding road through empty fields.
Warm spring wind, my heart conceals.

2
00:00:25,264 --> 00:00:32,607
Wild red poppies like fresh blood.
Church bell strikes the hour of six.

3
00:00:33,237 --> 00:00:41,064
Luna’s lips are soft and sweet,
My frozen cocoon starts to break.

4
00:00:41,195 --> 00:00:49,092
Tasting freedom, wings that beat,
A brand new hope begins to wake.

5
00:00:49,421 --> 00:00:57,422
But the lioness starts to cry
“Paul… I…” her broken word.

6
00:00:57,501 --> 00:01:06,371
I fold my wings, I cannot fly,
Lost in a shadow, cold and blurred.

7
00:01:14,821 --> 00:01:22,186
Sitting on the organ bench.
Hip to hip, our shadows clench.

8
00:01:22,576 --> 00:01:30,654
“Come with me for coffee, Paul.”
I just nod and look away.

9
00:01:30,816 --> 00:01:38,410
Cold door handle in the shed.
My frozen cocoon starts to break.

10
00:01:38,891 --> 00:01:46,669
Tasting freedom, wings that beat,
A brand new hope begins to wake.

11
00:01:46,914 --> 00:01:54,757
But the lioness starts to cry
“Paul… I…” her broken word.

12
00:01:54,804 --> 00:02:02,996
I fold my wings, I cannot fly,
Lost in a shadow, cold and blurred.

13
00:02:20,368 --> 00:02:27,907
Riding moped down the hill.
Wind is biting, sharp and chill.

14
00:02:28,084 --> 00:02:35,955
Other boys are dancing free.
Staring at a lonely bed.

15
00:02:36,269 --> 00:02:43,797
“I am done!” I scream out loud.
Shouting at the heavy cloud.

16
00:02:44,154 --> 00:02:52,247
Your church is empty, you are dead.
No one answers when I cry.

17
